Project: PolicyCompare — Frontend Prompt

Goal
- Generate a complete, production-friendly React frontend (Vite + TypeScript) using Material UI (MUI).
- UI must fetch policy data from a backend API and allow the user to select up to 4 policies to compare side-by-side.
- Clean, minimal, accessible, responsive design with good UX patterns.

Stack & Tooling
- Vite + React + TypeScript
- MUI v5 (components + theming)
- React Router
- SWR or React Query for data fetching (recommend React Query)
- ESLint + Prettier config

App Structure (generate these files + folders)
- src/
  - main.tsx (app entry, theme provider, router)
  - App.tsx (routes)
  - pages/
    - PolicyListPage.tsx (list with search/filter, multi-select)
    - PolicyComparePage.tsx (compare up to 4 policies side-by-side)
  - components/
    - PolicyCard.tsx (compact card for list)
    - PolicyTable.tsx (table layout for compare)
    - Header.tsx (top app bar, search, compare counter)
    - FloatingCompareTray.tsx (persisted bottom tray showing selected items)
  - services/
    - api.ts (fetch wrapper using fetch or axios)
    - policyClient.ts (typed methods: listPolicies, getPolicy, comparePolicies)
  - hooks/
    - usePolicies.ts (React Query hooks)
  - types/
    - policy.ts (Policy type interface)
  - styles/
    - theme.ts (MUI theme with light neutral design)
  - utils/
    - formatters.ts

Data & UX Requirements
- Policy type fields: id, title, description, effectiveDate, issuer, tags[], sections[] (section has title and content), lastUpdated, sourceUrl.
- PolicyList: support server-side pagination, client-side search, tag filtering, and multi-select (checkbox) for comparison.
- Comparison: when user selects 2–4 policies, allow side-by-side view showing key fields and sections aligned. Highlight differences.
- Limit selection to 4; show clear UI messaging when limit reached.
- Provide ability to export comparison as PDF (optional; include affordance and placeholder handler).

Accessibility & Performance
- Keyboard focusable items, semantic HTML, aria labels for compare tray and buttons.
- Lazy-load policy detail content in compare view (render summary first).

Dev & Run Commands (generate package.json scripts)
- `npm install`
- `npm run dev` — run dev server
- `npm run build` — production build
- `npm run lint` — ESLint
- `npm run format` — Prettier

Testing
- Provide basic unit tests for components using React Testing Library and a sample E2E test with Playwright or Cypress (one example test)

Integration Points
- API base URL configurable via `.env` (VITE_API_URL)
- Endpoints used (expected):
  - GET /api/policies  -> list (supports pagination, search, tags)
  - GET /api/policies/:id -> single policy
  - POST /api/compare -> accepts array of ids, returns combined comparison (optional; frontend can also fetch details individually)

Deliverables when this prompt is executed
- A ready-to-run Vite React TypeScript project with the described structure and components implemented, wired to call the specified backend endpoints, with instructions to run and test.

Notes for automated generator
- Prefer functional React components + hooks.
- Keep CSS-in-JS via MUI `sx` and `styled` only.
- Use TypeScript strict mode, include types for API responses.
- Add comments with TODO markers where human decisions may be needed (auth, advanced PDF export).

End of frontend prompt.